+The economic object here is operating revenue net of variable manufacturing
+cost, conditional on a project reaching commercialization. With elastic
+residual demand, the developer balances a higher margin against reduced
+sales. Higher marginal manufacturing cost raises the optimal product price
+and reduces the resulting operating-profit opportunity. Later organizational
+choices compare this opportunity with distinct setup, institutional and
+capacity costs. The present calculation alone neither selects a route nor
+predicts a change in project advancement or observed product counts.
